<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover"/><meta name="theme-color" content="#080808"/><title>The Wolf-Woman — 29</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden;background:#080808;color:#e4e3df;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}.dark-page{position:absolute;top:50%;left:50%;width:736px;height:1012px;transform:translate(-50%,-50%) scale(var(--dark-fit,1));transform-origin:center;background:#080808;overflow:hidden}.dark-page:after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none;opacity:.14;background-image:url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg viewBox='0 0 140 140' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg'%3E%3Cfilter id='n'%3E%3CfeTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='.8' numOctaves='3' stitchTiles='stitch'/%3E%3C/filter%3E%3Crect width='100%25' height='100%25' filter='url(%23n)' opacity='.18'/%3E%3C/svg%3E")}.dark-page .story{position:absolute;left:125px;top:343px;width:437px;margin:0;font:14.5px/22.5px Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;text-align:justify;letter-spacing:.03px}.dark-page .initial{width:100px;height:103px;float:left;margin:-23px 1px 0 -20px;object-fit:contain}.dark-page .branch{position:absolute;left:148px;top:795px;width:414px;height:100px;object-fit:contain}.rail{position:absolute;right:63px;top:0;height:1012px;border-left:1px solid #aaa9a5;width:1px}.rail:after{content:"";position:absolute;top:504px;left:0;width:64px;border-top:1px solid #aaa9a5}.folio{position:absolute;left:699px;top:487px;font:italic 14px Georgia,serif}.twig{position:absolute;left:700px;top:512px;font:22px Georgia,serif;transform:rotate(180deg)}
</style></head><body><main class="dark-page" aria-label="The wolf-woman, page 29"><p class="story"><img class="initial" src="/34/initial.png" alt="Illuminated T"/>he hunters approached the wolf-woman. The creature wept, the flow of her tears soaked into the earth – then in that moment, her form began to alter, to change into something new. Her coat split under the torrent of sobs, her flesh broke open and crystal-clear waters burst from her body. And under the astonished eyes of the hunters, the wolf-woman disappeared beneath the surge of her own tears. Her sides, her legs, her feet became a spring, and soon, having become a river, she swallowed up the hunters. Her waves washed across the stony paths. The song of the tree rose like a prayer through the iridescent waves, which in their turn sang to the same melody. Cascades of notes were swept along by the river, and fluttered about its banks. The lapping of the waters and the murmur of the waves mingled with this song of love, and the melody it gave birth to struck panic in the hearts of dwarves and mandrakes.</p><img class="branch" src="/34/branch.png" alt="Delicate botanical engraving"/><div class="rail"></div><span class="folio">29</span><span class="twig">♧</span></main><LightPage base="/34"/><script is:inline>function fit(){document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--dark-fit',Math.min(innerWidth/736,innerHeight/1012));document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--paper-fit',Math.min(innerWidth/816,innerHeight/1200));}addEventListener('resize',fit,{passive:true});fit();</script></body></html>
